    {
      "text": "rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom, Matt. 19:23. came a rich man of Arimathæa, Matt. 27:57. money … many that were rich cast in much, Mark 12:41. the rich he hath sent empty away, Luke 1:53. woe unto you that are rich, Luke 6:24. ground of a certain rich man brought forth plentifully, Luke 12:16. he that layeth up treasure … is not rich toward God, Luke 12:21. There was a certain rich man, which had a steward, Luke 16:1. rich man … clothed in purple and fine linen, Luke 16:19. very sorrowful: for he was very rich, Luke 18:23. rich men casting their gifts into the treasury, Luke 21:1. Lord over all is rich unto all, Rom. 10:12. Now ye are full, now ye are rich, 1 Cor. 4:8. as poor, yet making many rich, 2 Cor. 6:10. though he was rich, yet … he became poor, 2 Cor. 8:9. God, who is rich in mercy, Eph. 2:4. rich fall into temptation, 1 Tim. 6:9. Charge them that are rich … that they be not highminded, 1 Tim. 6:17. they be rich in good works, 1 Tim. 6:18. rich, in that he is made low, James 1:10. shall the rich man fade away in his ways, James 1:11. God chosen the poor of this world rich in faith, James 2:5. ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries, James 5:1. I know thy … poverty, (but thou art rich), Rev. 2:9. sayest, I am rich, and increased with goods, Rev. 3:17. causeth all, both … rich and poor, free and bond, to receive a mark, Rev. 13:16. merchants of the earth are waxed rich, Rev. 18:3.",
